## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow-like transform
function process(event) {
  if (!event || !event.id) return;
  if (!seen.has(event.id)) {
    writeBigQuery(event);
    seen.add(event.id);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant isolation at scale?
- How would you handle late-arriving data and replays?
- What are your rollback/disaster-recovery considerations?

Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of a practical, multi-tenant flag service using serverless components. It touches storage (Firestore), caching (Memorystore), security boundaries (per-tenant isolation), feature rollout semantics, and basic observability—areas often seen in production.

Key Concepts
- Serverless Cloud Run with endpoints
- Firestore per-tenant isolation
- Memorystore caching with TTL
- Percentage rollout logic
- Observability basics

Code Example
```javascript
function evaluateFlag(cfg, userId, rollout) {
  if (!cfg.enabled) return false;
  if (rollout && rollout.percentage != null) {
    const seed = hash(userId + cfg.flagName) % 100;
    return seed < rollout.percentage;
  }
  return cfg.value;
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you audit rollout behavior across tenants?
- How would you scale cache invalidate when a tenant updates config?
